A raw pool shell in an open compound. Bare laterite to the boundary, no shade,
and a fall running back toward the house — which meant every heavy rain put
water where nobody wanted it.

The owners wanted somewhere to sit in the afternoon, not just a pool to look
at. That turned a surfacing job into a garden: shade first, then planting to
hold the ground, then paving set to move water away rather than across.
